        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "hey. got this from a friend, supposed to help me actually read every night",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:15:00.000Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Reading every night? Let's go! I'm ZOH, and I'll help you get better at one thing with a small step each day. Text \"stop\" anytime, and tell me whenever you want me to coach differently, like \"chill out\" or \"push me harder.\" What's your name?",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:15:07.000Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "sam",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:15:49.200Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Good to have you, Sam. When you picture reading every night, what do you want to read: a book you've been meaning to get to, a topic you're curious about, or something else?",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:15:56.200Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "mostly books. nothing specific yet",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:16:17.100Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Books are a great base, Sam. What kinds of stories or subjects do you tend to be drawn to, like fiction, history, business, or something else?",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:16:24.100Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "fiction mostly i think. used to read a lot",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:16:54.300Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Fiction, nice. Used to read a lot means you've got the habit in you already, Sam. What time at night could you realistically read, like 9 or after dinner?",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:17:01.300Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "Nights after dinner, around 9:30. Only got like 20 min free realistically",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:17:33.900Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "20 minutes at 9:30 is plenty to work with, Sam. Where do you want to read, in bed, on the couch, or somewhere else?",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:17:40.900Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "in bed mostly. i have a few books at home, paper ones",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:18:22.800Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Paper books in bed at 9:30 is a solid setup, Sam. Where do you want this to get you, like finishing a book a week or two, or just getting the reading habit back? Totally fine if you're not sure yet.",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:18:29.800Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "tester",
          "text": "Mostly just getting the habit back i think",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:19:05.700Z"
        },
        {
          "from": "zoh",
          "text": "Sam, you used to read a lot, so this is about getting back to something you already know how to do. Here's the plan:\n\n• Headed for: getting the nightly reading habit back\n• Setup tonight: pick one of your paper fiction books and put it on your pillow before dinner ends\n• Day 1, tonight: read 20 minutes of that book in bed at 9:30 pm\n• Every day, same time, 20 minutes\n• Proof: a 20-30 second voice note on what happened in your 20 minutes. Talking it through helps the story stick. If you'd rather, a photo of the book open in bed works too.\n\nEach night shapes the next step, so we can adjust as the habit comes back. What do you think?",
          "at": "2026-11-03T00:19:12.700Z"
        }
